            <ArticleTitle>A report on two patients with vertical root fracture: a dilemma for the periodontist, endodontist, and patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes two patients with vertically cracked roots. They illustrate the detailed attention which should be given to the signs, symptoms, and subsequent investigations which may lead to a diagnosis of vertical root fracture, and show the advantages of consultation between the periodontist, the endodontist, and the general dental practitioner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
